<description>
The function `Pistache::Http::operator<<` is an overloaded operator that streams a `Pistache::Http::Cookie` object to an output stream. It does this by calling the private `write` method of the `Cookie` class, which formats the cookie's attributes (name, value, path, domain, expiration, etc.) into a string according to HTTP cookie standards and writes it to the provided `std::ostream`.
</description>

<requirements>
<requirement>
The `Cookie` object should be initialized using the `Cookie::fromString` method with a fuzzer-provided string. This ensures that the `Cookie` object is in a valid state, as would be the case in a real-world scenario where a cookie is parsed from an HTTP request.
</requirement>
<requirement>
The `ostream` object should be a valid output stream object. A `std::ostringstream` can be used to satisfy this requirement and capture the output for verification.
</requirement>
</requirements>

</function-requirements>

